                     | Concept                  | One-line answer                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Timeout**              | Stops waiting for a slow/unresponsive dependency after a defined time.                                                                                                                             |
| **Retry**                | Tries a failed operation again when the failure may be temporary.                                                                                                                                  |
| **Exponential Backoff**  | Waits progressively longer between retries to avoid overwhelming a failing service.                                                                                                                |
| **Idempotency**          | Ensures repeating the same request produces the same final result without unwanted duplicates.                                                                                                     |
| **Circuit Breaker**      | Stops sending requests to a repeatedly failing dependency to protect your system.                                                                                                                  |
| **Graceful Degradation** | Keeps core functionality working by reducing/temporarily disabling non-critical features when a dependency fails.                                                                                  |
| **When to use each**     | Timeout → slow dependency; Retry → temporary failure; Backoff → space retries; Idempotency → safe retries; Circuit Breaker → repeated failures; Graceful Degradation → keep core system available. |
| **Interview point**      | Reliable systems expect failures and use timeouts, controlled retries, idempotency, circuit breakers, and fallbacks to prevent cascading failures.                                                 |
